==Strategy==
At first glance, this stage appears to be a much more obnoxious version of [[Fish Hell (Insane)|Fish Hell]], but it isn't nearly as scary as it may seem. This is due to the Malevolent Island Cats' exploitable [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] trait, opening a window of opportunity for [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|anti-Aku units]]. Several options that are available, such as [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] and [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]]. [[Talents|Talented]] [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]] on the other hand, is proved to be not as successful due to the high damage per hit of Malevolent Islands and the mix of metal enemies.

Due to the damage of the Malevolent Islands' [[Death Surge]]s, their wide spawning range, and the fact that multiple of them will spawn throughout the fight, the use of [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|cats with Surge immunity]] is heavily advised in order for them to not incinerate your army. If you lack in Surge Immune units, disposable mid-rangers that can do lots of damage such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] can suffice as long as you manage your cash correctly. Due to Malevolent Island's Counter-Surge ability, [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attackers]] are generally ill-advised, since the stacked up Malevolent Islands can very easily send numerous surges across the field covering everything. While on the other malevolent stages you can use a fully surge immune lineup, there isn't really a viable Critical Hitter outside of Uber Rare category that is [[Immune to Surge]].

Additionally, due to the Malevolent Island Cats' Aku trait, there are a lot more crowd-control units that can target and mitigate their threat. Units such as [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]] will absolutely shine in this stage. Although they have a blind spot and need proper support to guard it, their [[Long Distance]] attacks work especially well since they can use the Metal enemies as stepping stones and keep knocking the Malevolent Islands back.

Do not forget to bring a [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitter]] for those pesky Metal Doges and the Super Metal Hippoe! The usual [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]] and [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] will work just fine, but may end up being inconsistent with the Malevolent Islands' Death Surges potentially wiping them out. [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] is an effective as a Critter here due to his range, provided you use Critical Chance UP [[Cat Combo]]s to make up for his low Crit rate.

Be sure to complete the stage within 8 minutes, or else a quintet of Sir Metal Seals will spawn, which can quickly lead to your downfall from DPS overload.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Imagawa Yoshimoto (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yoshimoto]]: With the target Aku Talent, it can almost perma-Weaken all the Islands (Can with a small Weaken Cat Combo), especially since they have no Shields to get in Yoshimoto's way. They even have Long Distance to hit them when the Metal peons and hippo are in the way. Although they don't have Surge Immunity, they are [[Strong Against]] them, so you will have another off cooldown typically before they die.
*[[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Devil Hunter Satoru]]: Treat them as a more reliable Fiend Cat. Essentially a hard counter to this stage, having 100% [[Slow]] and [[Knockback]] to all the Islands. Long Distance lets him hit enemies even while Metal peons are in the way. He also has Surge Immune, so very little in this stage can actually threaten him aside from the Metal peons. Just protect him and win.
*[[Amakusa Shiro (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Amakusa]]: At Lv.30, he can 2 shot the Islands, if all 6 hits from his 3-part multi attack land. As all the Islands all have 1 knockback, it's very easy to cripple a whole stack of Islands. He also has Surge Immunity and a large range advantage, but he can struggle with the Metal peons unless the Islands are lured into his range, which is dangerous.
*[[Shitakiri Sparrow (Uber Rare Cat)|Grand Chunchun Haunters]]: Alongside an amazing one slot cat combo that can help boost your cone cats, the guaranteed Knockback and Wave Attack is great crowd-control for disrupting the stacks of the Malevolent Island Cats. They attack so frequently that the Malevolent Islands will barely do enough damage to push forward before getting knocked back.
*[[Agent Staal (Uber Rare Cat)|Edgemaster Staal]]: If you have him, Staal can trivialize this stage with his abilities of both Crit and Slow against both [[Metal]] and Aku. Although his chance to perform a [[Critical Hit]] is very low at just 3% (can be made 5% with [[Miracle Performance (Combo)|Miracle Performance]]), his extreme attack speed combined with a 3-part [[Multi-Hit]] more than makes up for it. His Slow ability, again combined with his incredible hit rate, also lets him "Staal" everything nearly permanently. Both of these abilties are further enhanced by his 30% chance to create a level 3 [[Mini-Wave]], allowing him to proc on enemies hiding behind the frontline. To top it off, he outranges everything here, wields the Strong Against ability, and is Immune to Surge.

